CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 3 --no-assertions --datarace --yaml-witness -
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^- segment: \[{waypoint: {type: .function_enter., action: .follow., location: {file_name: .main.c., line: 14}, thread_id: 0}}\]$
^- segment: \[{waypoint: {type: .target., action: .follow., location: {file_name: .main.c., line: 15}, thread_id: 0}}, {waypoint: {type: .target., action: .follow., location: {file_name: .main.c., line: 7}, thread_id: 1}}\]$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
The YAML violation witness of a data race found by the round-robin encoding:
the read of x in main (line 15) and the write of x in the created thread
(line 7), together in one segment, after the creation of that thread. Under
--rounds the race assertion is made at the first step of the equation, so
its property id is not "datarace" (here it is `.recursion`): the witness
writer has to recognise the race by the assertion's comment, or it writes
no witness at all.
